#: patterns/faq.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Expandable questions and answers (core block “Details”)."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:15
msgid "Frequently asked questions"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:19
msgid "Which vehicles can I manage?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:21
msgid "Motorcycles, cars, bicycles, e-bikes, quads and scooters – as many as you like."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:27
msgid "How do the intervals work?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:29
msgid "For each job you set after how many kilometres and/or months it is due. Whichever is reached first counts. The app shows you what is due soon or already overdue."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:35
msgid "What is in the PDF report?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:37
msgid "The selected maintenance entries with date, mileage, work done, parts and costs – for your records or when you sell your vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:43
msgid "What is the difference between the portal and household mode?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:45
msgid "In the portal everyone has their own account with email address and password. Household mode is meant for your home network: no login, everyone picks their profile. That is why it must not be reachable from the internet."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:51
msgid "Is Bike Maintainer open source?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:53
msgid "Yes, under the MIT licence. The source code is on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:59
msgid "Which languages are available?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:61
msgid "German and English – for the interface, the emails and the PDFs. You choose the language in your account."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:67
msgid "Is there an app for my phone?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:69
msgid "Yes, for Android 10 or newer. It reminds you of due maintenance and lets you record work right at the vehicle. The APK is on GitHub; Obtainium keeps it up to date. It needs no Google services."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:75
msgid "What happens to the photos of the worksheets?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:77
msgid "The app reads the values on your phone. The photo is not uploaded – only the values you confirm are saved."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:83
msgid "Can I take my data with me?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:85
msgid "Yes. Every vehicle can be exported as a file with its tasks, entries and target values and imported again – in the portal or on your own server."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:91
msgid "Where can I ask questions?"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/faq.php:93
msgid "In the forum. Bugs and ideas are also welcome as issues on GitHub."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php
msgctxt "Pattern title"
msgid "Features"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php
msgctxt "Pattern description"
msgid "Nine features of the app as cards with icons, in three rows."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:17
msgid "Made in the workshop, for the workshop"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:21
msgid "For everyone who looks after their own vehicles"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:25
msgid "Everything you need to document the value and reliability of your vehicles without gaps."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:39
msgid "Intervals by mileage or time"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:43
msgid "Reminders by mileage or months – whichever comes first. See due and overdue work at a glance, and record extra work right along with the maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:55
msgid "Report and checklist as PDF"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:59
msgid "A complete maintenance report for your records or when you sell, plus a checklist for your next workshop visit."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:71
msgid "Parts and costs"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:75
msgid "Parts with quantity and price, labour costs and an overview for the current year and in total – in several currencies, too."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:91
msgid "Worksheets for the workshop"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:95
msgid "Print a worksheet for valve clearance, brakes, chain or tyres, fill it in by hand at the bike and photograph it with the app. Your phone reads the values – the photo never leaves it."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:107
msgid "Measured values and targets"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:111
msgid "Store the target values from the workshop manual. Values outside them are highlighted, and for shim-adjusted valves the app suggests the new shim."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:123
msgid "Take your data with you"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:127
msgid "Export a vehicle with its whole history as a file and import it elsewhere – from the portal to your own server or the other way round."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:143
msgid "Every kind of vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:147
msgid "Motorcycles, cars, bicycles, e-bikes, quads and scooters side by side, each with its own maintenance plan and history."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:159
msgid "For the whole household"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:163
msgid "In household mode everyone picks their profile – no password, in your own home network."
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:175
msgid "German and English"
msgstr ""

#: patterns/features.php:179
msgid "Interface, emails and PDFs are available in both languages, set per account."
msgstr ""

